From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: Probe the camera
 modules

Each camera connector carries one of two modules, which share its
supplies, reset line and MCLK. Mark the module nodes "fail-needs-probe"
so that the camera module prober enables the one that answers, instead
of having every sensor driver probe and the absent ones fail.

The prober drives the MCLK and reset pins of the rear connector before
any sensor node is enabled, so have the pin controller hold them, as it
holds those of the front connector.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi  | 23 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi
index 7de5ce49b7..bd629db171 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi
@@ -223,13 +223,13 @@ voice_coil_motor: vcm@c {
 	 * driver while powered), LDO2_C 1.8V (dovdd), GPIO92-gated core rail
 	 * (dvdd), reset GPIO7, MCLK4.
 	 * The upstream ov13b10 register tables assume a 19.2 MHz MCLK.
+	 * The camera module prober enables the node of the module that
+	 * answers; the pins are held by the pin controller, see &tlmm.
 	 */
 	camera_rear: camera@36 {
 		compatible = "ovti,ov13b10";
 		reg = <0x36>;
-
-		pinctrl-0 = <&camr_rgb_default>;
-		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		status = "fail-needs-probe";
 
 		clocks = <&camcc CAMCC_MCLK4_CLK>;
 		assigned-clocks = <&camcc CAMCC_MCLK4_CLK>;
@@ -280,6 +280,7 @@ &cci2_i2c1 {
 	camera_front: camera@20 {
 		compatible = "hynix,hi846";
 		reg = <0x20>;
+		status = "fail-needs-probe";
 
 		clocks = <&camcc CAMCC_MCLK3_CLK>;
 
@@ -309,14 +310,13 @@ hi846_ep: endpoint {
 	/*
 	 * The other front camera module (Xinli S5K4H7, fixed focus), with the
 	 * same supplies, reset GPIO and MCLK3 as the HI846. Only one of the two
-	 * is fitted: the driver of the missing one finds no sensor at its
-	 * address and releases the supplies and the reset GPIO (a shared GPIO,
-	 * through the gpio-shared proxy) for the other. The pins are held by
-	 * the pin controller, see &tlmm.
+	 * is fitted, and the camera module prober enables the node of the one
+	 * that answers. The pins are held by the pin controller, see &tlmm.
 	 */
 	camera_front_s5k4h7: camera@2d {
 		compatible = "samsung,s5k4h7";
 		reg = <0x2d>;
+		status = "fail-needs-probe";
 
 		clocks = <&camcc CAMCC_MCLK3_CLK>;
 
@@ -349,11 +349,12 @@ s5k4h7_ep: endpoint {
 
 &tlmm {
 	/*
-	 * The front camera's MCLK and reset pins are configured here rather
-	 * than by a sensor node: both front sensor nodes use them, and this
-	 * pin controller lets only one device own a pin.
+	 * The cameras' MCLK and reset pins are configured here rather than by
+	 * a sensor node: the camera module prober drives them before any
+	 * sensor node is enabled, and two sensor nodes use those of each
+	 * connector, while this pin controller lets only one device own a pin.
 	 */
-	pinctrl-0 = <&camf_rgb_default>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&camf_rgb_default>, <&camr_rgb_default>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 
 	cam_indicator_en: cam-indicator-en-state {
